From 0d82d2e7821f08e1a5ab2905f45004d053d72f02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:42:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(edm): wire verify and the wire-iso post read an open
 run as open

The open runs of #1109 (side left / right of travel) meet #534's wire
laws and #1139's wire-iso post:

- sim::verify::wire gains CutSide::Open: the kerf law judges the run
  against the part at every height (a kerf that touches the part is a
  gouge and blocks the post); the start-hole and slug laws are skipped
  with the reason on the verdict (OPEN_SKIP) and the report line; both
  ends must stand clear of the stock by the kerf (OpenEndInStock).
- The verify gate maps left / right to Open and no longer refuses an
  open run for its missing start hole.
- wire-iso.cps threads at the run-in point and cuts the wire at the
  run-out (operator notes say so without AWT); it writes the path's
  moves only, so no return move exists. Closed goldens unchanged.

Pinned by an_open_cutoff_posts_its_golden_and_a_gouging_one_is_refused
(new golden nc/wire-iso/wire_contour_open_cutoff.nc) and
an_open_run_is_judged_by_its_kerf_with_no_start_hole_or_slug.

Refs #1109

